insert into public.quick_reference_sections (id,body,version)
values ('antihypertensive-bolus','| Medication | Adult IV dose · timing · pertinent details |
|---|---|
| **Labetalol** | **Perioperative small bolus: 2.5–10 mg over 2 min**; individualized anesthesia dosing, not the labeled severe-hypertension escalation regimen. Onset 5–15 min. ([Perioperative review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148691/)) **Labeled severe hypertension:** 20 mg over 2 min, then 40–80 mg every 10 min as needed; **300 mg cumulative maximum**. Peak effect usually within 5 min of each labeled injection; effect persists for hours. Avoid asthma, severe bradycardia, greater-than-first-degree block, overt HF/cardiogenic shock. ([Prescribing information](https://labeling.pfizer.com/ShowLabeling.aspx?id=4492)) |
| **Hydralazine** | **5 mg slow IV** is a low-dose perioperative option; this differs from the larger labeled 20–40 mg dose. Onset **5–20 min**; effect often **2–6 h**, potentially longer. ([Perioperative review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148691/); [Label](https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=f1a10203-f027-4f9c-8dd6-907c6db24d47&type=display)) Published perioperative repeat interval **20–60 min**; reassess before redosing because peak may take **10–80 min** and the effect is unpredictable. ([Perioperative dosing review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2515421/)) Reflex tachycardia; contraindicated in CAD and rheumatic mitral valve disease. ([Label](https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=f1a10203-f027-4f9c-8dd6-907c6db24d47&type=display)) |
| **Esmolol** | **Gradual control: 500 mcg/kg (0.5 mg/kg) over 1 min**, then infusion if needed. **Immediate perioperative control: 1 mg/kg over 30 sec**, then 150 mcg/kg/min if needed; select regimen by clinical urgency and hemodynamics. ([Brevibloc label](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/019386s053lbl.pdf)) Onset **1–2 min**; effect roughly **10–30 min**. ([Perioperative review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148691/); [BP review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4178624/)) Watch bradycardia, hypotension, AV block, decompensated HF and bronchospasm; do not suppress compensatory tachycardia from hypovolemia. ([Label](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/019386s053lbl.pdf)) |
| **Metoprolol tartrate** | **2.5–5 mg IV over 1 min**; may repeat every **2–5 min** to **15 mg total**, titrating to BP/HR response. Peak response about **20 min**; duration **5–8 h**, so avoid rapid dose stacking. ([Hospital IV manual](https://pdtm.vch.ca/Documents/metoprolol%20NEW.pdf)) **IV use for hypertension is off-label in the US**; the US injection label is for stable acute MI, not a general BP protocol. Avoid significant bradycardia/block, hypotension and decompensated HF; caution with bronchospasm. ([US label](https://labeling.pfizer.com/ShowLabeling.aspx?id=17205)) |','2026-09-27')
on conflict (id) do update set body=excluded.body,version=excluded.version,updated_at=now();

