insert into public.quick_reference_sections (id,body,version)
values ('antihypertensive-infusion','| Medication | Adult IV infusion · titration · pertinent details |
|---|---|
| **Nicardipine (Cardene)** | Start **5 mg/h**; increase by **2.5 mg/h every 5–15 min**; **maximum 15 mg/h**. Onset within minutes; about **50% offset in 30 min**, with residual effect potentially lasting hours. Watch reflex tachycardia, hypotension and phlebitis; **contraindicated in advanced aortic stenosis**. ([Prescribing information](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/022276Origs027lbl.pdf)) |
| **Clevidipine (Cleviprex)** | Start **1–2 mg/h**; initially may double every **90 sec**. Near goal, use smaller increases every **5–10 min**. Usual **4–6 mg/h**; most patients ≤16 mg/h; **32 mg/h only limited short-term experience**. Onset **2–4 min**; offset **5–15 min**. **Do not exceed 1,000 mL/24 h** (label average limit 21 mg/h); count other lipid sources. Contraindicated with **egg/soy allergy, defective lipid metabolism, or severe AS**. Discard vial **12 h after puncture**. ([Prescribing information](https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=f9290625-b723-4eda-bab8-a97bef6041f6&type=display)) |
| **Esmolol (Brevibloc)** | Gradual control: after **500 mcg/kg over 1 min**, start **50 mcg/kg/min for 4 min**; titrate stepwise to **100, 150, then 200 mcg/kg/min**, reassessing at 4-min steps. **Hypertension may require 250–300 mcg/kg/min**; >300 not studied. **Tachycardia maintenance >200 mcg/kg/min is not recommended.** Immediate perioperative regimen: **1 mg/kg over 30 sec**, then **150 mcg/kg/min** if needed. Monitor ECG/BP; avoid bradycardia/block, decompensated HF, shock, and closely timed IV verapamil. ([Prescribing information](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2023/019386s053lbl.pdf)) |
| **Labetalol** | Label example: **2 mg/min**, adjusted to BP response; usual effective total **50–200 mg**, up to **300 mg**. Effect persists for hours; not a rapid-offset infusion. Keep supine and assess orthostatic tolerance before ambulation. Avoid asthma, severe bradycardia/block and overt HF/cardiogenic shock. ([Prescribing information](https://labeling.pfizer.com/ShowLabeling.aspx?id=4492)) |
| **Nitroglycerin (NTG)** | Start **5 mcg/min** with non-adsorptive tubing; increase by **5 mcg/min every 3–5 min** to 20 mcg/min, then increments of **10–20 mcg/min** if needed; smaller/slower changes after response. **No universal maximum in the label**: follow local limits. Infusion only; concentrated product must be diluted. ([Label](https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=b8af0974-33ea-4dd5-9ff7-3b61272aeb25&type=display)) Onset **2–5 min**, offset about **3–5 min**; mainly venodilates. ([BP review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4178624/)) **Contraindicated with PDE5 inhibitors or riociguat**. ([FDA](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2014/019970Orig1s015ltr.pdf)) Caution in preload-dependent states/RV infarction. ([NTG review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9278720/)) |
| **Sodium nitroprusside (SNP)** | Start **0.3 mcg/kg/min**; assess BP for **at least 5 min** before retitration. **Maximum 10 mcg/kg/min**; keep exposure as short as possible. Onset **1–2 min**; hypotensive effect resolves in **1–10 min** after stopping. Continuous BP monitoring and infusion pump required. Cyanide risk increases above **2 mcg/kg/min**; hepatic dysfunction increases risk. For **eGFR <30**, mean rate **<3 mcg/kg/min**; for **anuria**, mean rate **≤1 mcg/kg/min**. Avoid PDE5 inhibitors/riociguat; consider ICP and thiocyanate accumulation. ([Prescribing information](https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2018/209387s004lbl.pdf)) As a conservative perioperative ceiling, **10 mcg/kg/min for <10 min**, not a maintenance rate. ([Perioperative review](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2515421/)) |','2026-09-27')
on conflict (id) do update set body=excluded.body,version=excluded.version,updated_at=now();

